Installing Kernel, Modules, and Host Build Binaries

1. Create the boot directory in your target environment:

`mkdir -p /boot`

2. Copy the Gentoo binary kernel and initramfs images from the host system into /boot:

`cp -av /boot/vmlinuz* /boot/`
`cp -av /boot/initramfs* /boot/`

3. Copy the compiled kernel modules to match your kernel version:

`cp -av /lib/modules/* /lib/modules/`

4. Copy GNU Make binary from host system into target /usr/bin:

`cp -av /usr/bin/make /usr/bin/`

5. Verify that the kernel, modules, and build binary are in place:

`ls -lh /boot`
`ls -lh /lib/modules`
`make --version`
